WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.022
Now compare the two sides.

00:00:03.022 --> 00:00:06.417
On the left are raw log its such as 4.1, 3.4, and 2.8.

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:12.392
Soft max transforms those scores into a probability distribution.

00:00:12.392 --> 00:00:20.302
On the right, the candidates now have interpretable probabilities such as forty-eight percent, twenty-four percent,

00:00:20.302 --> 00:00:22.794
and thirteen percent.

00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:26.701
The Python code does the same thing with a real model.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:34.901
We take the last-position log its, apply soft max, select the top candidates, and decode their token I D's so we can

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:38.040
inspect what the model is considering next.
